ffplay: hardware decoding without the Vulkan renderer, frames copied to memory

ffplay 8.1 takes -hwaccel only together with its Vulkan renderer (libplacebo, a Vulkan surface for the window). On
macOS with StrixArc's RADV there is neither: RADV decodes on VCN but cannot present to a Cocoa window. Without the
renderer the decoder now gets a device of its own (as ffmpeg's -hwaccel does) and every decoded frame is copied to
memory (av_hwframe_transfer_data) for the SDL renderer, as mpv's *-copy hwdecs do. NV12, what hardware decoders hand
over, goes straight into an SDL NV12 texture (SDL 2.0.16+) instead of through swscale to YUV420P.
-hwaccel_opts passes options to that device, e.g. avoid_host_import=1: copies through FFmpeg's pooled staging buffers
instead of importing each frame's memory, which costs a kernel round trip per frame on some drivers (StrixArc's).

